# interplay_life_delay_finish_suspend: A Delay (61) never signals, and every lifecycle call that drains the FIFO holding it waits for it forever: pause, rvg_device_finish_suspend (rvg_device_will_suspend only quiesces, and returns), stop, reset, release (the device's shutdown stops it) and recreate (which releases first), with the Delay on the root FIFO; pause and rvg_device_finish_suspend with it on a child FIFO. Each hangs at that call: the watchdog fires there. rvg_device_will_suspend alone is locked returning, and a NOP rung after it is not run.
